    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `FailureHandler.detect_failure()` is not idempotent per `(model_id, round_idx)` and will double-count duplicate deliveries/retries by appending to `_perf_history[model_id]` on every call. Location: `detect_failure()`, UNDERPERFORM branch. Evidence: `self._perf_history.setdefault(response.model_id, []).append(perf)` runs unconditionally whenever the response is non-empty, non-timeout, parseable, and format-compliant. In a distributed system, retries happen and a timeout does not imply failure; if the same round is processed twice, the persistence window is advanced artificially, making `UNDERPERFORM` fire earlier than the actual round history warrants. This is a boundary-relevant correctness defect because the immune layer consumes `failed` state derived from these recovery decisions.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND-FIX-FOLLOW\nFIND: `FailureHandler.detect_failure()` appends performance observations directly to a list with no per-round deduplication. Duplicate processing of the same response/round therefore mutates future failure classification. Evidence: `_perf_history` is `Dict[str, List[float]]`, and the code has no `(model_id, round_idx)` guard before `append(perf)`.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n        # Performance history for underperformance detection\n        self._perf_history: Dict[str, List[float]] = {\n            m.model_id: [] for m in models\n        }\n>>>>\n====\n        # Performance history for underperformance detection.\n        # Keyed by round to make failure detection idempotent under retries.\n        self._perf_history: Dict[str, Dict[int, float]] = {\n            m.model_id: {} for m in models\n        }\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n        # Priority 5: UNDERPERFORM (with persistence window)\n        perf = self._performance_metric(response)\n        self._perf_history.setdefault(response.model_id, []).append(perf)\n\n        h = self.config.persistence_window\n        recent_perfs = self._perf_history[response.model_id][-h:]\n        if len(recent_perfs) >= h:\n            underperform_count = sum(\n                1 for p in recent_perfs if p < self.config.theta_under\n            )\n            if underperform_count / len(recent_perfs) >= self.config.eta_underperform:\n                return FailureType.UNDERPERFORM\n>>>>\n====\n        # Priority 5: UNDERPERFORM (with persistence window)\n        perf = self._performance_metric(response)\n        model_perf_history = self._perf_history.setdefault(response.model_id, {})\n        model_perf_history[response.round_idx] = perf\n\n        h = self.config.persistence_window\n        recent_rounds = sorted(model_perf_history.keys())[-h:]\n        recent_perfs = [model_perf_history[r] for r in recent_rounds]\n        if len(recent_perfs) >= h:\n            underperform_count = sum(\n                1 for p in recent_perfs if p < self.config.theta_under\n            )\n            if underperform_count / len(recent_perfs) >= self.config.eta_underperform:\n                return FailureType.UNDERPERFORM\n>>>>\nFOLLOW: This fix has downstream interface consequences. (1) Any code that inspects `_perf_history` as a list must be updated to treat it as `Dict[int, float]`; within the visible artifact only `detect_failure()` reads it, so no additional in-boundary call sites are shown. (2) Because duplicate rounds no longer inflate persistence, `get_recovery()` will be invoked less aggressively for `UNDERPERFORM`; this changes escalation timing and may reduce `DOWNGRADE_ROLE` frequency. (3) The same idempotency problem still exists separately in `_failure_history` / `get_recovery()` recording; this fix does not solve duplicate failure-record insertion, so repeated recovery decisions for the same round can still distort repetition counts even after perf-history deduplication.",
