    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND-FIX-FOLLOW\nFIND: `FailureHandler.should_abort()` derives PM identity from the current mutable `role_map` instead of preserving the original PM model id. This makes the PM-abort rule depend on mutable routing state. Evidence: `for mid, role in self.role_map.items(): if role == Role.PM: pm_id = mid` is executed each call, after `get_recovery()` may already have changed roles.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n        self.role_map = role_map\n        self.config = config\n        self.event_callback = event_callback\n>>>>\n====\n        self.role_map = role_map\n        self.config = config\n        self.event_callback = event_callback\n        self._pm_model_id = next(\n            (mid for mid, role in role_map.items() if role == Role.PM),\n            None,\n        )\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n        pm_id = None\n        for mid, role in self.role_map.items():\n            if role == Role.PM:\n                pm_id = mid\n                break\n\n        if pm_id is not None and pm_id not in self._active_models:\n            return True\n>>>>\n====\n        pm_id = self._pm_model_id\n        if pm_id is not None and pm_id not in self._active_models:\n            return True\n>>>>\nFOLLOW: This fix affects all semantics that rely on PM identity. (1) `get_recovery()` PM special handling still checks `is_pm = self.role_map.get(model_id) == Role.PM`; that should be changed to `model_id == self._pm_model_id` to keep classification consistent with `should_abort()`. (2) Any external code that mutates `role_map` to reassign PM mid-run will now diverge from `FailureHandler`’s preserved PM identity; if dynamic PM reassignment is actually intended, that requires an explicit API to update `_pm_model_id` under controlled rules. (3) The validator `validate_k1()` continues to pass under this change and becomes a stronger check of the static-PM invariant.",
