\"{model_id}: cost-per-finding {current_cpf:.1f}s \"\n                            f\"exceeds 2σ (mean={mean_cpf:.1f}s, σ={std_cpf:.1f}s)\"\n                        ),\n                        severity=\"WARNING\",\n                        recommended_action=(\n                            f\"Model {model_id} efficiency collapse: spending \"\n                            f\"{current_cpf:.0f}s per finding vs historical \"\n                            f\"{mean_cpf:.0f}s. Consider reducing prompt complexity, \"\n                            f\"adjusting decomposition, or benching temporarily.\"\n                        ),\n                        evidence={\n                            \"model_id\": model_id,\n                            \"current_cpf\": current_cpf,\n                            \"mean_cpf\": mean_cpf,\n                            \"std_cpf\": std_cpf,\n                            \"threshold\": mean_cpf + 2 * std_cpf,\n                            \"occurrence\": persistence + 1,\n                        },\n                    )\n                    self._diagnoses.append(diag)\n                    results.append(diag)\n>>>>\n====\n                cpf_key = f\"cpf_spike_{model_id}\"\n                if std_cpf > 0 and current_cpf > mean_cpf + 2 * std_cpf:\n                    persistence = self._pathology_counts.get(cpf_key, 0)\n                    self._pathology_counts[cpf_key] = persistence + 1\n                    diag = DetectorDiagnosis(\n                        detector=\"cpf_spike\",\n                        pathology=(\n                            f\"{model_id}: cost-per-finding {current_cpf:.1f}s \"\n                            f\"exceeds 2σ (mean={mean_cpf:.1f}s, σ={std_cpf:.1f}s)\"\n                        ),\n                        severity=\"WARNING\",\n                        recommended_action=(\n                            f\"Model {model_id} efficiency collapse: spending \"\n                            f\"{current_cpf:.0f}s per finding vs historical \"\n                            f\"{mean_cpf:.0f}s. Consider reducing prompt complexity, \"\n                            f\"adjusting decomposition, or benching temporarily.\"\n                        ),\n                        evidence={\n                            \"model_id\": model_id,\n                            \"current_cpf\": current_cpf,\n                            \"mean_cpf\": mean_cpf,\n                            \"std_cpf\": std_cpf,\n                            \"threshold\": mean_cpf + 2 * std_cpf,\n                            \"occurrence\": persistence + 1,\n                        },\n                        pathology_key=\"cpf_spike\",\n                    )\n                    self._diagnoses.append(diag)\n                    results.append(diag)\n                else:\n                    if self._pathology_counts.get(cpf_key, 0) > 0:\n                        self._resolved_counts[cpf_key] = (\n                            self._resolved_counts.get(cpf_key, 0) + 1\n                        )\n                        if cpf_key not in self._remediation_state:\n                            self.record_natural_resolution(cpf_key)\n                        self._pathology_counts[cpf_key] = 0\n>>>>\nFOLLOW: This fix has two downstream effects. (1) `false_positive_rate` will now receive additional natural-resolution events for parser/cpf incidents, which will further stress its denominator approximation; that exposes an existing self-diagnosis calibration defect rather than introducing a new one. (2) Adding `pathology_key` to these diagnoses means `apply_diagnosis()` can start routing them into remediation chains; if `_REMEDIATION_CHAINS` lacks `parser_yield` or `cpf_spike`, that completeness gap becomes active and must be resolved consistently.",
